Friday's clothes left the S&amp;P 500 at 7376.86, up 23.13 points, after a session that also

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:57.818
swung with US midterm election results. The NASDAQ composite finished Friday at 24,579.42,

00:00:57.818 --> 00:01:07.738
2, up 264.43 points, up 5.78% year-to-date, and up 9.86% since the practice portfolio opened

00:01:07.738 --> 00:01:09.638
on March 16, 2026.

00:01:10.518 --> 00:01:20.398
The S&amp;P TSX composite rose 183.82 points to 35,789.09, while the Dow Jones industrial

00:01:20.398 --> 00:01:31.138
average finished down 237.33 points at 51,285.73. The Canadian dollar traded at 70.86 cents

00:01:31.138 --> 00:01:38.938
US, down from 71.48 cents the prior session. December crude oil rose 31 cents to 90 US dollars

