and $0.90.

00:01:47.678 --> 00:01:53.361
Rate-sensitive groups such as REITs and Financials showed mixed leadership this week, while

00:01:53.361 --> 00:01:57.361
those Bank of Canada and Federal Reserve decisions stay the frame around the tape.

00:01:58.041 --> 00:02:05.401
XEI tracks the S&amp;P-TSX composite high dividend index at a 3.5% distribution yield, and

00:02:05.401 --> 00:02:10.361
the Motley Fool Canada notes that a single ticker replaces the chore of rechecking and rebalancing

00:02:10.361 --> 00:02:15.781
individual dividend names for regular tax-free savings account, or TFSA contributors.

00:02:16.461 --> 00:02:20.881
ZRE follows an equal weight Canadian real estate investment trust, or REIT,

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:26.881
basket at a 4.7% yield, so each trust gets a similar allocation at rebalancing,

00:02:27.301 --> 00:02:31.721
and the mix is not hostage to the largest holding. Held in equal dollar amounts,

00:02:31.941 --> 00:02:35.981
those two monthly payers are like stuffing a rent envelope from two different paychecks.

00:02:36.301 --> 00:02:39.581
If one check is light, the other still lands on the first of the month,

00:02:39.581 --> 00:02:42.741
and you never had to recruit extra hours from a third job.

00:02:43.241 --> 00:02:48.641
An investor opens a TFSA at a platform such as Questrade or WealthSimple, contributes

00:02:48.641 --> 00:02:54.221
the capital, buys equal dollar amounts of each exchange traded fund, or ETF, and sets

00:02:54.221 --> 00:02:57.601
the account to reinvest or withdraw the distributions every month.

00:02:58.101 --> 00:03:04.761
A $200 Canadian monthly tax-free target at that blended rate needs roughly $58,500 Canadian

00:03:04.761 --> 00:03:12.341
dollars in total capital. Because 2,400 Canadian dollars of annual distributions divided by 0.041

00:03:12.341 --> 00:03:18.581
produces that figure. The approach has delivered steady income in sideways or modestly rising Canadian

00:03:18.581 --> 00:03:24.001
markets, and it can lag when broader equity rotation favors growth stocks over yield names,

00:03:24.381 --> 00:03:29.761
which is exactly what showed up in recent sessions when financials and REITs underperformed tech.

00:03:29.761 --> 00:03:35.101
To implement it, screen for monthly payers in the brokerage interface, confirm the current

00:03:35.101 --> 00:03:39.761
yields on the ETF fact sheets, and size the position so the blended payout meets the

00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:42.361
target monthly amount after that yield calculation.

00:03:43.347 --> 00:03:49.347
International business machines, ticker IBM on the NYSE, unveiled its most advanced quantum

00:03:49.347 --> 00:03:54.127
computer in Chicago, and that hardware event is the catalyst for today's simulated weekly

00:03:54.127 --> 00:03:54.567
hold.

00:03:55.007 --> 00:03:59.187
This is a simulated trade for learning purposes, with no real money involved.

00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:03.087
The structure is a covered call on a $1,000 US dollar position.

00:04:03.607 --> 00:04:08.387
Entered at Monday's open under the published rules, held five sessions and judged against

00:04:08.387 --> 00:04:12.127
the NASDAQ over that same window, with no discretionary exit.

00:04:12.747 --> 00:04:17.527
Price sits above the 50 session average, an announcement day volume ran above the 20-day

00:04:17.527 --> 00:04:17.867
average.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:22.747
A close back under that 20-day moving average on volume still above average would kill

00:04:22.747 --> 00:04:25.307
the catalyst thesis before the stop ever has to.

00:04:25.307 --> 00:04:31.947
The stop sits 8% below entry, which caps the simulated loss at $80 USD, and the target

00:04:31.947 --> 00:04:36.227
is 2% to 5% including call premium over the five-session window.

00:04:36.667 --> 00:04:41.487
Confidence is low, a single catalyst factor with no sector rotation confirmation yet.

00:04:41.967 --> 00:04:46.747
Because quantum hype can fade quickly, and yesterday's closed income hold already told

00:04:46.747 --> 00:04:49.847
us not to upgrade a thesis when the sector is not confirming.

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:53.247
That low grade is the sector rotation filter talking.

00:04:53.247 --> 00:04:58.547
We are not treating IBM as a weak dividend name, but we still refuse to talk ourselves

00:04:58.547 --> 00:05:03.787
into medium when rotation has not shown up, which is the same discipline that rule is testing.

00:05:04.487 --> 00:05:08.947
Unlike the blended yield construction, this overlay harvests a short-term event premium

00:05:08.947 --> 00:05:10.627
rather than a monthly distribution.

00:05:11.167 --> 00:05:15.667
You own the shares, you sell a call against them, you keep the premium, and at the end of

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:19.887
the window either the shares are called away if prices through the strike, or you keep

00:05:19.887 --> 00:05:21.707
the shares in the premium if it is not.

00:05:21.707 --> 00:05:28.747
early assignment is not modeled, the hold runs to the fifth session's close, or the stop, whichever comes first,

00:05:29.327 --> 00:05:32.987
and listeners who want the missing premium number will pull it themselves in a minute.

00:05:34.102 --> 00:05:40.242
KMP.UN, the geographically diversified apartment-reat trading below book value with monthly distributions,

00:05:41.202 --> 00:05:45.922
was the simulated weekly hold that ran five sessions from Monday's open to Friday's close.

00:05:45.922 --> 00:05:52.042
We simulated buying it at 17 Canadian dollars and 8 cents at that Monday open, and exiting

00:05:52.042 --> 00:06:01.482
at 17 Canadian dollars and 65 cents at Friday's close, again of 3.34% or $33.37 on the $1,000

00:06:01.482 --> 00:06:02.102
position.

00:06:02.702 --> 00:06:10.042
The NASDAQ fell 3.99% over those same five sessions, so the hold produced 7.33% of alpha,

00:06:10.542 --> 00:06:13.822
and honestly that feels pretty good on a low confidence income name.

00:06:13.822 --> 00:06:19.502
Stated confidence was low, the 8% stop was never reached, and the invalidation

00:06:19.502 --> 00:06:24.442
never mattered. Price simply drifted higher on steady distributions while broader rotation

00:06:24.442 --> 00:06:29.562
pressured other sectors, so the low grade fit the mix setup, and the income thesis held

00:06:29.562 --> 00:06:35.042
up. The adjustment I would make next time is simple. Require sector rotation confirmation

00:06:35.042 --> 00:06:40.042
before entering any dividend name already showing relative weakness, even when the monthly

00:06:40.042 --> 00:06:45.710
cache still looks tidy on the fact sheet. Interactive brokers surfaces live listed options

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:51.830
for any US equity with enough liquidity, so you can quote exact strikes, expires, and premiums

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:57.590
before you commit capital to a covered call, or a cache secured put. Canadian users get that

00:06:57.590 --> 00:07:03.250
chain data through an IBKR account with no extra fee, and the edge is seeing real-time implied

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:08.930
volatility and open interest rather than estimated premiums. Volume and open interest figures

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:13.450
on the same screen tell you whether a chosen strike actually has enough liquidity for the

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:18.290
expiry you want, which is the difference between an overlay you can exit and one you only

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:19.070
hope to exit.

00:07:20.083 --> 00:07:24.883
Comparing several expires side by side is how you spot where premium decay accelerates,

00:07:25.323 --> 00:07:29.423
and that is the field you read when you are structuring a five-session catalyst overlay

00:07:29.423 --> 00:07:31.163
like the simulated IBM call.

