00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:26.893
You hold ZDRE inside a TFSA, and the monthly distribution hits, and it is easy to treat

00:10:26.893 --> 00:10:28.533
every dollar like bond interest.

00:10:29.253 --> 00:10:34.533
Read distributions flow through as return of capital, income, or capital gains, and inside

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:39.873
At a TFSA, none of those categories triggers immediate tax, unlike a non-registered account

00:10:39.873 --> 00:10:45.473
where return of capital reduces adjusted cost-base and can create future capital gains exposure.

00:10:46.133 --> 00:10:51.713
The BMO equal weight REITS index ETF pays monthly, and those payments retain their character

00:10:51.713 --> 00:10:56.313
even when sheltered, so the tax label does not vanish just because the account does.

00:10:57.013 --> 00:11:02.973
Download the annual tax information package each REIT or ETF publishes in February and confirm

00:11:02.973 --> 00:11:07.813
the split before filing, rather than assuming every dollar is pure income. The

00:11:07.813 --> 00:11:12.533
misconception is that all REIT payouts behave like bond interest. The fix is to

00:11:12.533 --> 00:11:16.433
treat them as a three-part allocation and track the capital component separately,

00:11:16.933 --> 00:11:21.413
even inside registered accounts. So you still know the true economic return if

00:11:21.413 --> 00:11:26.113
you ever move the holding outside the TFSA or need adjusted cost base for any

00:11:26.113 --> 00:11:31.684
reason. Open your brokerage options chain for IBM, locate the nearest monthly

00:11:31.684 --> 00:11:37.224
expiry and note the premium for a 5% out of the money call, divide that premium by the

00:11:37.224 --> 00:11:41.544
current share price and annualize it to see the income yield a covered call structure

00:11:41.544 --> 00:11:46.224
would have delivered this week. Before we wrap, Monday's open is when rate sensitive

